WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
On Sundays, in churches across the world,

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.190
people stand and speak the same words.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.460
I believe in God the Father
Almighty, Maker of heaven and earth.

4
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:16.090
This is a creed, from the
Latin credo: I believe.

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.320
An early form was written
down in Rome by about 340.

6
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:24.880
So why do Christians all over the world
still say words first written down over

7
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.940
1,600 years ago?

8
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.770
In this mission, you'll read the
Apostles' Creed line by line,

9
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.330
and decode old words like quick and Ghost.

10
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.580
Then you'll find where creeds
turn up in Christian life,

11
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.980
from baptisms to funerals.

12
00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:45.950
Your mission: find out why Christians
still say these ancient words today.
